Z||000000||Lynx||10-19-1999||04:07 AM||||I just thought of a idea today and wondered if anyone has did or seen someone do this. I was thinking of putting some kind of scoop on the hood down low by the radiator that would pour more air around the radiator and look pretty cool. Do you all think im dumb or think it would be cool. Like just a small scoop, not tall but long from side to side.||||reg||6
Z||000001||lowCG||10-19-1999||11:12 AM||||If you open up the hood,it will provide a route for air/heat to escape from behind the radiator,works on my car,the opening starts about 6" from the front of the hood,is the shape the structure underneath provides.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-19-1999||03:56 PM||||I've seen several people take the hood "vents" from Firebird GTA's and place then in the center just behind the radiator.  It gives the air a place to go(if you haven't noticed, GM didn't do a very good job of allowing the air out once it's gone through the radiator).  This allows the engine to run cooler, plus it prevents the headlight covers from opening up on high speed cruises.||||reg||3
